+# D1 read exhaustion fix
+
+Prepared on 29 October 2026. No production settings, campaigns, inboxes or billing were changed.
+
+The every-minute reply mailbox query can start from every sent step for each connected inbox. A synthetic SQLite fixture with 1,500 sent recipients assigned to one of 10 inboxes reproduced the repeated work. Recipient-first lookup and a covering steps index reduced the mailbox selector from 121,698 to 210 SQLite VM instructions while selecting the same mailbox. This is a local execution-work measurement, not a measurement of production D1 rows_read. Live Cloudflare query insights remain necessary to establish incident attribution.
+
+Changes:
+- Drive reply lookup from each inbox's recipients, then look up sent steps.
+- Scope campaign completion checks to each campaign's recipients.
+- Skip delivery selection when no running, non-test live/draft campaign is eligible.
+- Drive the scheduler's inbox-priority query from campaigns and recipients.
+- Add indexes for recipient/step state lookups and unresolved attempt checks.
+
+No schedule, sending cap, reply-stop, opt-out, reservation or uncertain-delivery behavior is relaxed. The free plan stays configured.
+
+Validation completed: TypeScript check; hosting preflight; SQLite query plans, mailbox choice and completion checks with pending, inflight, uncertain and failed work.
+
+Validation blocked: Miniflare/Vitest needs a localhost listener, which this task's sandbox rejects with EPERM. The original 90-test suite and new read-budget regression therefore need to run outside this sandbox. Remote query insights failed because the stored Cloudflare CLI session expired and its authentication server was unreachable here.
+
+## Apply and release
+
+From the real mailer repository, apply the supplied patch with `git apply --check` first, then `git apply`. Run:
+
+```sh
+npm run check
+npm test
+python3 scripts/check-d1-query-plans.py
+npm run preflight
+```
+
+Reconnect Cloudflare with `npx wrangler login` if needed. Inspect database read metrics and obtain query insights:
+
+```sh
+npx wrangler d1 insights DB --sort-by reads --sort-type sum --json
+```
+
+After daily quota resets (30 October, 00:00 GMT), apply the additive index migration before deploying the Worker:
+
+```sh
+npx wrangler d1 migrations apply DB --remote
+npm run deploy
+```
+
+The migration builds indexes and itself consumes read/write allowance. The Worker change uses ordinary SQL and is compatible with the previous schema if a deployment ordering issue occurs. Do not upgrade billing automatically. Review uncertain/inflight attempts in the app before manually resuming any paused inbox; never reset them to pending in bulk.
+
+Compare subsequent D1 row-read totals and query insights with the previous period. The free account has a shared 5-million-row daily budget across all its D1 databases, so inspect other databases too.
